  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Triple Canopy obligated $324M in FY2026 to date across 66 awards, with an average award size of $4.9M and obligations down 14.6% year over year. Triple Canopy received the largest share of its FY2026 obligations from the Department of Homeland Security, which obligated $221M, followed by the Department of State with $91.7M and the Department of Defense with $11.6M. Security Guards and Patrol Services is Triple Canopy's dominant market at $282M in FY2026 to date. Security Systems Services (except Locksmiths) accounted for $23.6M, Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services accounted for $15.6M, and Engineering Services accounted for $3.1M. Historical obligations show year-to-year variation: FY21 was $479M, FY22 was $382M, FY23 was $468M, FY24 was $478M, and FY25 was $380M. The current-year totals are partial because the period is fiscal year to date. This snapshot highlights where agency demand and market focus concentrated for Triple Canopy so far in FY2026 and how current obligations compare to prior fiscal years.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated is Triple Canopy's FY2026 business by agency?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security is the largest buyer, obligating $221M. The Department of State is the second-largest buyer, obligating $91.7M. The Department of Defense is a smaller buyer in FY2026, obligating $11.6M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets drive Triple Canopy's revenue in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Security Guards and Patrol Services is the largest market at $282M. Security Systems Services (except Locksmiths) is next at $23.6M, followed by Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services at $15.6M and Engineering Services at $3.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
